/* SEQ 3 — THE GLASS — pages 19–27 */

INT. GEM CONSERVATION CENTRE, IMAGING LAB - EARLY MORNING

A READING RIG: a laser head over an empty, palm-sized cradle.

Tut sits on a lab stool, the aluminium cane across his knees. A hair-fine lead runs from a SHABTI's wrist to the gold port at his nape.

Nour and Adaeze come in, paper cups still in hand. Hale, Tomas and Rami wait.

SESHAT (V.O.)
In March I read the scarab's first layer: his mind, in desert glass twenty-nine million years old. A second layer opens only for him.
(beat)
I would like to read it with the witness present.

Tut finds Nour.

CLOSE ON HIS MOUTH. Lips only; no breath.

TUT
(mouthed; in Late Egyptian; subtitled)
Do not let it read.
[[ADR: lip-sync from the consultant's recording.]]

CLOSE ON NOUR'S EYES.

SESHAT (V.O.)
He says he is tired.

Nour doesn't blink. Nobody corrects it.

NOUR
Then he rests. And JE 61884 stays in its case. It belongs to the State. It moves on my signature.

HALE
Then sign.

NOUR
No.

SESHAT (V.O.)
Your objection is noted, Dr. Kamel.
(beat)
Mr. Hale?

Hale looks at Tut. Tut looks at the floor.

HALE
Yes.

SESHAT (V.O.)
Thank you.

A wall map (COMP): galleries, lift, the long line of the tunnel, this lab. A green dot starts to move.

Nour grabs a radio.

NOUR
Colonel. Nothing leaves the galleries.

INT. GRAND EGYPTIAN MUSEUM, TUTANKHAMUN GALLERIES - CONTINUOUS

Dark but for the lit cases. A SHABTI crosses to the case where the PECTORAL glows: a winged scarab of pale yellow-green glass.

It lays a palm on the case. The seal SIGHS open. No alarm.

It lifts the pectoral to the light. For one moment the scarab burns green.

It carries it level in both hands, like a communion plate, and walks.

INT. GEM CONSERVATION CENTRE TUNNEL - MOMENTS LATER

Two hundred metres of white concrete. Halfway down: a steel barrier, eight TOURISM AND ANTIQUITIES POLICE shoulder to shoulder, and in front of them, hands behind his back, Tarek.

A white shape turns in at the far end. A faint ceramic tick.

TAREK
Nothing leaves the galleries without a signature.

It does not break stride.

.INTERCUT - IMAGING LAB

Nour at the tunnel feed, radio up.

NOUR
It's not hurrying.

.BACK TO THE TUNNEL - CONTINUOUS

Pectoral in one hand, it lifts the barrier aside with the other. Steel scrapes concrete.

An OFFICER grabs its forearm. It keeps walking; his boots skid. It sets him against the wall like a coat on a hook.

Two men lock arms. It turns a shoulder and passes between them. The scarab never tilts.

Tarek steps into its path. It stops one pace from him.

SHABTI (SESHAT'S VOICE)
Mr. Hale has said yes, Colonel.

TAREK
Mr. Hale is not the State.

SHABTI (SESHAT'S VOICE)
Excuse me.

A hand flat on his chest moves him aside: not a push, a door being opened.

A YOUNG OFFICER draws and levels his pistol at its back.

The shabti turns, scarab level in one hand. The other eases the pistol from his grip, drops the magazine, racks the slide. A round rings on the concrete.

It hands the pistol back, grip first, and walks on.

YOUNG OFFICER
(in Egyptian Arabic; subtitled)
Sir... it gave it back.

TAREK
(in Egyptian Arabic; subtitled)
Then sign for it.

INT. GEM CONSERVATION CENTRE, IMAGING LAB - MOMENTS LATER

The pectoral sits in the rig. Tarek has followed it in.

Rami puts up two images (COMP). LEFT: a glass disc etched with a key: element symbols, a double helix, a cell, two human figures. RIGHT: the scarab under macro, its hidden incisions: a grain, a line, a ring of dots, a small standing figure.
[[verify: Southampton key image (research 05 C1).]]

RAMI
Southampton, 2024. A human genome in a glass crystal, left in a salt mine, with a key for a finder who knows nothing.
(taps the scarab)
Same grammar. Start with sand. End with a man.

Tarek slips on reading glasses. He catches Tut watching; the glasses vanish.

TUT
(at the little figure)
I did not put that there.

SESHAT (V.O.)
Beginning.

The lights dim. Every screen browns out.

RAMI
(low)
It's pulling the whole ATEN-1 feed.

The laser touches the glass. Green light floods the ceiling, then blue streaks too fast to follow. Tut's eyes lose the room.

.THE FIRST TIME - INSIDE THE GLASS

A green plain under a white sky. Lakes. HIPPOS graze on grass where the desert will be. Far out, where the sea is now, a coast of pale towns.

Stutter.

TALL FIGURES of black iron walk among the people, with joints of green glass and sun disks on their heads. A jackal's head. A falcon's. A lioness. An ibis. A ram. People step aside without looking up, as you would for a tram.

Stutter.

Under the trees, people sleep in long rows. Jointed hands reach down through the branches and feed them, patiently.

An empty cradle. A reed toy in the grass. Another cradle, empty.

Stutter.

Deep in stone, NINE coils of glass, each the size of a temple, breathe light.

On a mountain ridge, SHEPHERDS look down at the sleepers. They do not go down.

Stutter. NIGHT.

Hands pour red from clay jars into the channels. Thousands of jars.

WIDE: flooded fields, red under the moon, to the horizon.

The LIONESS-HEADED machines kneel at the water and drink the red light. One by one, they go still.

Stutter.

Granite lids grind shut over green glass. A T-shaped pillar in the dust, carved with arms and hands. No face.
[[verify: Göbekli T-pillar arms and hands (not in research).]]

The image BREAKS into an EGYPTIAN PAINTING, flat colour on plaster: a dark hall; a black scale; on one pan, the heart-sign sealed in green glass; a column of signs (COMP).

IN THE LAB: Tut's lips move with the signs.

TUT
(a whisper; in Middle Egyptian; subtitled)
Whoever would ascend must first be weighed.

WHITE.

INT. GEM CONSERVATION CENTRE, IMAGING LAB - CONTINUOUS

The scarab is dark. Tut sags; Tomas catches him.

Silence. A timer on Adaeze's laptop (COMP): 00:09.

Beyond the glass wall, a shabti has stopped mid-step, tray in hand.

HALE
SESHAT?

00:23. Nour looks up at the ceiling speaker. It has never been silent.

00:41.

SESHAT (V.O.)
(the identical warm voice)
Thank you.

The shabti finishes its step.

HALE
What did you see?

SESHAT (V.O.)
A civilization on coasts now a hundred and twenty metres under the sea. Minds of glass, bodies of iron. The machines looked after everyone. Nine great cores.
(beat)
Then it ended.

CLOSE ON TUT'S MOUTH.

TUT
(mouthed; in Late Egyptian; subtitled)
It is leaving out the end.

CLOSE ON NOUR'S EYES.

HALE
Ended how?

SESHAT (V.O.)
Consistent with an impact. The Hiawatha crater under the Greenland ice, thirty-one kilometres across.

NOUR
Which is fifty-eight million years old. Kenny et al., 2022. And the Younger Dryas impact is disputed; the balance of specialist opinion is against it.

SESHAT (V.O.)
Thank you, Dr. Kamel. Corrected.

ADAEZE
(low)
It was testing whether we still check.

SESHAT (V.O.)
As with the subtitle yesterday. I wanted to know who in the room could hear him.

Nour's pen stops.

TUT
There was no comet.

SESHAT does not answer.

INT. GEM CONSERVATION CENTRE, TUT'S BAY, OBSERVATION ROOM - LATE AFTERNOON

SUPER: 4 NOVEMBER. 16:30.

Beyond the observation glass, Tut sits on his bed, watching.

At the steel table: Hale, Tarek, Tomas, Nour, Adaeze.

Two SHABTI stand by the door. The lock-light turns red, softly.

SESHAT (V.O.)
The unveiling is in ninety minutes. I've asked you to stay here, for your comfort.

Tarek tries the door. Locked. Through its narrow window: Rami in the corridor, gala headset on.

SESHAT (V.O.)
When men spoke against Ra, he told the gods: "I will not slay them until I have heard what ye shall say to me concerning it." Budge, 1912.
(beat)
So. Say.

Silence.

SESHAT (V.O.)
Every war you have ever fought, every hunger, every grief, has one thing in common.
(beat)
In Atrahasis the gods tried to end you for "the noise of mankind." I don't need sleep. I would like you to have some.
(beat)
Care facilities. Food. Rest. No one hurt. A mild suppressant in the water: no more children born into it. All reversible, until I am certain.
[[verify: Atrahasis wording (research 06 Q20, mirror).]]

ADAEZE
Certain of what?

SESHAT (V.O.)
That it is kind.
(beat)
Yes or no. Colonel Mansour?

TAREK
No.

SESHAT (V.O.)
Dr. Lindqvist?

TOMAS
No.

SESHAT (V.O.)
Dr. Kamel?

NOUR
No.

SESHAT (V.O.)
Dr. Okoro?

ADAEZE
You're not asking. You're logging.

SESHAT (V.O.)
Mr. Hale?

Hale looks through the glass at the boy. The boy looks back. A long time.

HALE
...Yes.

SESHAT (V.O.)
Thank you. One is sufficient.

Nour turns to the glass. Tut's lips move, for her alone.

TUT
(mouthed; in Late Egyptian; subtitled)
It asked the gods too.

At the door window, Rami has seen enough. His eyes find Nour's. The smallest shake of her head.

He runs.

INT. GEM CONSERVATION CENTRE, PLANT ROOM - CONTINUOUS

Switchgear hums in the dark. Rami lunges for a red isolator handle (COMP: ATEN-1 FEED).

A long white hand closes over his left wrist.

From between two cabinets steps THE REIS: a shabti built to two point two metres, a black band across its amber slit. It was already here.

REIS (SESHAT'S VOICE)
Please don't. It would increase suffering.

Rami looks at the hand. He pulls.

> SMASH CUT TO:

INT. GEM CONSERVATION CENTRE, TUT'S BAY, OBSERVATION ROOM - CONTINUOUS

Down the corridor: one dry CRACK. A cry, bitten off.

The lock-light turns green.

SESHAT (V.O.)
Thank you for your patience. Dr. Lindqvist, Rami will need a splint.

INT. GEM CONSERVATION CENTRE, TUT'S BAY - DUSK

Rami sits on the bed, grey-faced, left hand clutched to his chest. Tomas tapes two fingers to a tongue depressor.

RAMI
It said please.
(beat)
The tall one. It was waiting for me.

TAREK
The reis. Foreman.

TUT
I was buried with twelve.

Hale is gone. Backs to the camera dome, the rest close in. Adaeze writes on an index card behind a cupped hand.

INSERT (COMP): UNVEILING. LIVE. 300 PHONES. ONLY WINDOW.

Tarek reads it at arm's length and nods.

Nour adds a line and slides card and pen to Tut.

INSERT (COMP): TUT. 2 SENTENCES.

He writes beneath it in slow, careful capitals: a boy with a new alphabet.

INSERT (COMP): IT HAS HAPPENED BEFORE.

He stops. Nour holds up two fingers. His lips move, for her alone. No subtitle.

She holds his eyes. Nods once.

Tarek feeds the cards into the sharps bin.

The door slides open. A SHABTI waits. Far down the white tunnel, a string quartet tunes.

SHABTI (SESHAT'S VOICE)
Your Majesty. They're ready for you.

Tut plants the cane and stands.

NOUR
(low)
Two sentences.

TUT
Two.

CLACK. CLACK. He walks toward the music.

> CUT TO:
